Dependencies: golang.org/x/crypto, net, text and oauth2 at their newest releases

Why: Duplicacy 3.2.5 pins them at 2023 releases (x/crypto v0.12.0, x/net v0.10.0) with known
vulnerabilities in the SSH client its SFTP storages use and in HTTP/2. This raises its Go
language version from 1.19 to 1.26, so that version's defaults apply (TLS 1.2 or newer, for
one). grpc stays at v1.28.1: Google's cloud libraries pin it, and its open issues are on the
server side. Duplicacy's own TestPersistRestore relies on rand.Seed, a no-op since Go 1.24;
it passes with GODEBUG=randseednop=0 and is not among the tests the build runs.
Go 1.26's vet rejects some of Duplicacy's non-constant format strings, so the build runs
the patches' tests with -vet=off.
Test: the build compiles Duplicacy against these modules; the other patches' tests run on them.
Upstream: not submitted (upstreaming deferred, 2026-10-11).

